    "result_text": "Done. The build compiles cleanly (regenerating the DTOs from the updated `openapi.yml`) and all tests pass.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature, keyed off the existing `POST /api/owners` pipeline and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back the acceptance test uses:\n\n1. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper (matching the existing `Luhn`/`CustomerCode`/`Sha256` pattern) that classifies completed years between a birth date and a reference date into `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when no birth date is present.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with accessors, plus a `@Transient` derived `getAgeBand()` that delegates to `AgeBand.classify(birthDate, registrationDate)`, sitting alongside the other derived getters (`getLocality`, `getContactPreference`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to `OwnerFields` and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to `Owner`. The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks both up automatically by property name, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n## Why it works\n\n`birthDate` flows request \u2192 `Owner` (via the existing `BuildOwner`/mapper) \u2192 persisted. `ageBand` is derived on read from the stored `birthDate` against the owner's `registrationDate` (which already defaults to the server date when unsupplied), so the create-then-GET round trip in `coreDerivesAgeBand` returns `ADULT` for a 1990 birth date. When no `birthDate` is supplied, `getAgeBand()` returns `null` and the field is simply omitted.\n\nI placed the classification logic in its own helper rather than inlining it in the entity, keeping `Owner` from accumulating band-boundary logic and leaving it reusable.",
